were healthy.
Mathlola (Brassicaceae). M. incana germ. 70L(84\% in 2nd w)i 70D(60\% in
2nd w), and 40(61\% in 3-7 w).
Meconopsis (Papaveraceae).
M. aculeata germ. 70L(64\% in 3-5 w) and none in 70D, 40-70L, or 40-70D. A 7
w period in 70D was fatal.
M. betonicifolia and the alba form germ. 70D(70\% in 3rd w). Light, GA-3, or a
